'# Digital Personal Data Protection Notice\n\n**Effective Date:** September 2026\n**Statutory Baseline:** Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act) and DPDP Rules, 2025.\n\n### 1. Who We Are\nDriving License Form ("Platform", "we", "us") is an independent citizen facilitation platform assisting applicants with driving and learner licence application preparation for Gujarat, Rajasthan, and Uttar Pradesh.\n\n### 2. What Personal Data We Collect\nWe collect only personal data necessary for your licence application:\n- **Identity & Demographics:** Name, date of birth, gender, father/guardian name, blood group.\n- **Contact Information:** Mobile number (verified via OTP), email address.\n- **Address Information:** Current and permanent address with postal PIN code.\n- **Supporting Documents:** Age proof, address proof, passport photograph, signature.\n- **Technical & Security Data:** IP address, session timestamps, audit logs.\n\n### 3. Why We Collect It & Lawful Basis\n- **Service Processing (Consent):** Form filling and document packaging for RTO dispatch.\n- **Identity Verification (Legal Requirement):** Ensuring statutory age and eligibility under the Motor Vehicles Act.\n- **Transactional Alerts (Consent):** SMS and tracking updates on application status.\n- **Security & Fraud Prevention (Legitimate Use & Legal Obligation):** Ensuring account integrity.\n\n### 4. Data Sharing & Third-Party Processors\nYour data is shared strictly with authorized partners: State RTO Authorities, RBI-regulated Payment Gateways, and TRAI-compliant SMS gateways within India. We NEVER sell or monetize citizen data.\n\n### 5. Your Statutory Rights as a Data Principal\nYou have the right under DPDP Act 2023 to:\n- **Access:** Review your stored personal data anytime at `/account/privacy`.\n- **Correction & Completion:** Correct outdated or erroneous details.\n- **Erasure:** Request deletion of personal data where statutory retention has ended.\n- **Consent Withdrawal:** Withdraw consent for optional processing.\n- **Nomination:** Designate another individual to act on your behalf.\n- **Grievance Redressal:** Raise complaints directly to our Grievance Officer.\n\n### 6. Grievance Officer & Data Protection Officer Contact\n**Officer:** Shri Animesh Sharma, Data Protection Officer\n**Email:** dpo@drivinglicenceform.in | privacy@drivinglicenceform.in\n**Address:** Privacy & Compliance Cell, Driving License Form, Gandhinagar, Gujarat 382010.\n**Response SLA:** Acknowledged within 24 hours, resolved within statutory timelines.',
'Comprehensive DPDP-compliant notice explaining data collection, processing purposes, sharing, citizen rights, and grievance officer details.',
'["application_processing","identity_verification","service_communication","payment_processing","document_verification","security","legal_compliance"]',
'["identity","contact","address","biometric","documents","financial"]',
